  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Hard boundary",
      "items": [
        "Server is a generic audio API — it does not know the robot exists",
        "Robot is a generic audio client — it does not know STT/LLM/TTS exist",
        "Only the audio contract is shared: WAV · 16kHz · mono · int16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Cognitive path",
      "items": [
        "Controller returns an immutable response plan before any generation",
        "Safe plans never reach the LLM, legacy memory, or a candidate proposal",
   "A memory offer or answer needs the face and the voice of the same person on that turn's own clip, never a token; otherwise the turn is the ordinary one",
        "Ollama is the only accepted LLM/VLM runtime (ADR-0004), reached only through one transport module",
        "A generic turn names its speaker by face or an observed token (never voice); the identified person gets one in-process session, an unknown speaker suspends it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Known gaps",
      "items": [
        "No liveness or replay defense: a photo identifies at basic; photo + recording would reach strong",
        "Reserved data needs strong assurance but no reserved capability is wired: propose, read and confirm each have one spoken consumer (the candidate dialogue) and correct and forget none; replay is measured, not defended; a PIN grant is bound to one operation but still proves the PIN, not the speaker (ADR-0015)",
        "Conversational memory is partial: short-term continuity (CM-2) and a default-off candidate dialogue (CM-3a, Plans 0062 and 0063: a taste is proposed, offered and promoted by voice); no retrieval (CM-5) or correction (CM-6); CM-0 baseline RED"
      ]
    }
  ]
